I would like to make some suggestions concerning NetHack.

The next version should be totally rewritten, but the older version V3.0
should be retained for novice players.
This does not mean that the older version should be ignored. There should
be patches to fix any bugs; however, any new ideas should go into the new
version.

Why should the next version be rewritten?
Consider why we play NetHack in the first place. NetHack is the only mainframe
game that requires ingenuity of the player and at the same time offers
unpredictability. When we first played NetHack, weren't you surprised that
you could do such things as sacrifice at an altar, drink from a fountain,etc.
You couldn't do such things in other games. For experienced players we would
like to see more stuff like that. It is this essence that gives a game 
playability. After we become familiar with what can be done, the game becomes
less thrilling and monotonous. 

Sure, rewriting the scenario isn't as simple as it seems, but I am sure
that the development team wrote V3.0 because of the challenge of programming.
So, I am sure they will take up the burden of writing a new game.

These are some suggestions concerning the new version:

* There should be some mail address at the development team so that any
  suggestions won't be lost and so that the suggestions could be organized.
  Anybody who wanted to see the list could do so. The list should also 
  contain why or why not the suggestion should be included; moreover, not
  just one reason each but all the reasons. I have seen some good ideas
  like blessed sharpening stones, chemists, etc., but all these ideas
  become lost in past news. In fact, players could vote on what to include
  and what not to include.

* There should be more monsters, lots more. Each monster's qualities should
  be well thought out. The difference between playing a game on brute
  strength and intelligence on the player is the monster's qualities. If
  the monster were to have every type of immunity (poison, ...), when the
  player encounters that monster he would have to throw things at it or
  fight it out, which depends alot on strength.

* More named monsters and weapons. I suggest looking in a thesaurus if 
  necessary.

* A more improved data base. The existing data base is lousy. If you
  identify a monster, some of the remarks are useless. Some remarks are
  the same for each monster. Alot of players are interested in the 
  history concerning monsters such as Demogorgon. At least a reference
  should be provided so that the player can look up information on the 
  monster. Also some information on identified items would be nice. Some
  players identify the item, but don't even know what it is. (Refer to 
  news on Athame)

* There should be a water level containing only water monsters. There 
  would be some special thing on that level which would attact the 
  player to that level such as treasure, sunken ships, vampire mermaids,etc.
  The same could be said for a air, earth, etc level.

* The player should be able to gain acid resistance from eating a monster.
  This of course makes cockatrices useless, but maybe somebody can think
  of something to solve this problem.

* Finally, pythons are not venemous. So, why should they be poisonous?


